    [bugfix] support encoder-decoder model state on MRV2 (#18044)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    The downstream MRV2 model state initializer overrides the upstream
    routing logic, causing cross-attention encoder-decoder models such as
    Cohere ASR to fall back to the default Ascend model state.
    
    Add an Ascend encoder-decoder model state that reuses the upstream
    encoder-decoder lifecycle while building Ascend-specific attention
    metadata.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce *any* user-facing change?
    
    None.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Added unit tests for model state routing and Ascend attention
    metadata.
    - Passed Ruff lint, format, Python compilation, and diff checks.
    - Upstream vLLM: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/44568
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
    Signed-off-by: wenshanchao <wenshanchao@huawei.com>

